      "writtenOn": "2020-12-11T06:32:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Potentially. The tradeoff is simplicity and that having a single freelist enforces order for the actual freeing, but it does have the potential for contention. Though I\u0027m not sure if the heap usage is likely to be cpu-affined so I\u0027m not sure breaking it up into multiple per heap lists will really provide much additional parallelism?\n\nWe could do per-heap kthread/shrinkers, but it adds to what the users of the library have to track (initialization calls, and a per-heap structure to be passed to the deferred_free call).",
